Subject: [PATCH 39/42] tests/e2e: MT golden-flow Playwright spec + page-object
 rename followup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds tests/e2e/features/multi-tenant/golden-flow.spec.ts: a single
end-to-end Playwright test that exercises the full multi-tenant
happy path against a live cluster:

  - login + create tenant on first sign-in
  - add openai-shaped custom provider (qwen3-coder Service URL)
  - add provider key with the model allow-list (real bearer secret)
  - create a Virtual Key with budget + token rate-limit
  - intercept the create POST to capture the one-shot VK secret value
  - hammer /v1/chat/completions until a quota tripping or the budget
    is exercised; assert >=1 successful 200 along the way
  - assert log rows render in /workspace/logs (Stage 4 tenant_id
    stamping)
  - create a team with its own budget; reassign VK to team via API
  - replay calls to confirm the limits keep firing

Env knobs default to the bm cluster fixture
(bm-llms-qwen3-coder.llm-system.svc.cluster.local:8000, model
qwen3.6-coder, bearer clowntown123) but are env-overridable so the
same spec can run against other LLM fixtures.

Also flips the governance page-object's "Create Customer" button
regex to "Create Namespace" — patch 0038 renamed the dialog title
display-only, but the existing page object matched the old text.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
